oku. It usually contains beef, onions, and button mushrooms in a thick demi-glace sauce often made with red wine and tomato sauce. This sauce is served atop or alongside steamed rice. The sauce is sometimes topped with a drizzle of fresh cream. Variants of the recipe sometimes include soy sauce and sake."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-hayashi-rice"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hayashi_rice"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Yoshoku","cuisine/yoshoku"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":7,"links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Demi-glace","ingredient/demi-glace"],["Mushroom","ingredient/mushroom"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Red wine","ingredient/red-wine"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Tomato sauce","ingredient/tomato-sauce"]]},{"h":"More from Yoshoku","links":[["Chicken katsu","dish/chicken-katsu"],["Cream stew","dish/cream-stew"],["Doria (food)","dish/doria-food"],["Menchi-katsu","dish/menchi-katsu"],["Naporitan","dish/naporitan"],["Rengatei","dish/rengatei"],["Tonkatsu","dish/tonkatsu"],["Volga rice","dish/volga-rice"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/d/d8/Hayashi_rice.jpg/500px-Hayashi_rice.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Hiratake at Japanese Wikipedia","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hayashi_rice.jpg"}},"dish/kindzmarauli":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/kindzmarauli","n":"Kindzmarauli","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Georgian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Kindzmarauli is a dark red, naturally semi-sweet Georgian wine. It is made from an indigenous grape variety of Saperavi from Kakheti region of the country."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-kindzmarauli"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kindzmarauli"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Georgian cuisine","cuisine/georgian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Geo