zzeria_Regina%2C_Boston_MA.jpg/500px-Pizzeria_Regina%2C_Boston_MA.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"John Phelan","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pizzeria_Regina%2C_Boston_MA.jpg"}},"dish/risalamande":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/risalamande","n":"Risalamande","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Risalamande is a traditional Danish dessert served at Christmas dinner and julefrokost (Christmas lunch). It is made of rice pudding mixed with whipped cream, sugar, vanilla, and chopped almonds. It is served cold with either warm or cold cherry sauce (kirsebærsovs)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-risalamande"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Risalamande"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Danish cuisine","cuisine/danish-cuisine"],["Norwegian cuisine","cuisine/norwegian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Almond","ingredient/almond"],["Cream","ingredient/cream"],["Rice pudding","ingredient/rice-pudding"],["Vanilla","ingredient/vanilla"],["Whipped cream","ingredient/whipped-cream"]]},{"h":"More from Danish cuisine","links":[["Æbleflæsk","dish/blefl-sk"],["Æbleskiver","dish/bleskiver"],["Danish pastry","dish/danish-pastry"],["Glögg","dish/glogg"],["Hvidsten Inn","dish/hvidsten-inn"],["Kokkeriet","dish/kokkeriet"],["Kransekage","dish/kransekage"],["Kringle","dish/kringle"],["Labskaus","dish/labskaus"],["Rødgrød","dish/r-dgr-d"],["Smørrebrød","dish/sm-rrebr-d"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/1/19/Risalamande.jpg/500px-Risalamande.jpg","w":500,"h":486,"by":"Malene Thyssen","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Risalamande.jpg"}},"dish/skyline-restaurant":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/skyline-restaurant","n":"Skyline Restaurant","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from American cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Skyline Restaurant (formerly The Speck and nicknamed \"The Skyliner\") is a diner in northwest Portland, Oregon, in the United States. Established in 1935, the restaurant initially sold fried chicken by a gas station. It gained popularity during the 1950s, and Skyline's menu of American cuisine has changed little since then. Michelle Nelson has owned the diner since 1999; previous owners have included Benny and Phyllis Lum, as well as Ken Hom, who eliminated drive-in service. Skyline's burgers and milkshakes have received a generally positive reception. In 1975, James Beard said the restaurant's burger was among the best in the country, and Food Network Magazine said Skyline had the best burger in Oregon in 2009."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-skyline-restaurant"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skyline_Restaurant"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from American cuisine","links":[["5-8 Club","dish/5-8-club"],["Altabira City Tavern","dish/altabira-city-tavern"],["Angel food cake","dish/angel-food-cake"],["Applebee's","dish/applebee-s"],["Arby's","dish/arby-s"],["Arnold's Bar and Grill","dish/arnold-s-bar-and-grill"],["Banana bread","dish/banana-bread"],["Banana pudding","dish/banana-pudding"],["Barbecue sauce","dish/barbecue-sauce"],["Be Our Guest Restaurant","dish/be-our-guest-restaurant"],["Beer cake","dish/beer-cake"],["Ben's Chili Bowl","dish/ben-s-chili-bowl"],["Benjy's","dish/benjy-s"],["Besaw's","dish/besaw-s"],["Better than sex cake","dish/better-than-sex-cake"],["Blackhawk (restaurant)","dish/blackhawk-restaurant"],["Blini","dish/blini"],["Blooming onion","dish/blooming-onion"],["Bobcat Bite","dish/bobcat-bite"],["Boiling Springs Tavern","dish/boiling-springs-tavern"],["Brix Tavern","dish/brix-tavern"],["Brown Betty (dessert)","dish/brown-betty-dessert"],["Brown Derby","dish/br